  "explanation": "The first mismatch occurs at cycle 6 where m_axis_tvalid is 0 but should be 1. This indicates the rate limiting logic is pausing output incorrectly. The condition gate at line 128 (patch_bdf206843497) qualifies the pause condition with !rate_by_frame, which directly addresses the rate_by_frame=1 test scenario where frame-based rate limiting should behave differently. Patches f46dec541b44 and c73ed0d6214c further refine the frame pause condition with !rst and s_axis_tvalid qualifications respectively, preventing spurious pauses during reset or when input is invalid. The rhs_substitution patches (1d0fba8d5d53, 3642db1cc528, 302bdac6f760, cde52ea68e59) improve signal initialization and forwarding logic for the output pipeline registers, ensuring valid data propagates correctly when not paused. The condition_gate patch 87d9d2ff8bbd adds s_axis_tvalid check to the accumulator threshold comparison, preventing rate limiting from triggering on invalid input cycles."
